# Deploy Supabase after changes

When finishing work that affects Edge Functions, shared domain/contracts/llm used by Edge, or anything the hosted Generate My Plan path calls:

1. Run `pnpm sync:edge` if `packages/domain`, `packages/contracts`, `packages/validation`, or `packages/llm` changed.
2. Deploy the affected Supabase functions (prefer full `npx supabase functions deploy` when unsure which functions bundle `_shared`).
3. Do this in the same turn as the code change — do not wait for the user to ask — so Vercel preview builds can hit the updated backend immediately.

Skip only when the change is purely mobile UI / docs / tests with no Edge or `_shared` impact.

Migrations: if SQL migrations were added, also apply them to the linked remote project (`npx supabase db push` or the repo’s documented migration path) before telling the user the change is ready to test.
